msgid "hardware.hint.title"
msgstr "Hint stage %d/%d"

msgid "hardware.hint.scope.1"
msgstr "Only fixed terminals are shown; no solution topology is revealed."

msgid "hardware.hint.scope.2"
msgstr "Only the key components and wires are shown; the rest is still yours to build."

msgid "hardware.hint.scope.3"
msgstr "The complete reference topology is shown along its real displayed wires."

msgid "hardware.hint.reveal_next"
msgstr "View hint stage %d"

msgid "hardware.hint.returned"
msgstr "Returned to your workbench “%s”."

msgid "hardware.hint.generic"
msgstr "Use the inputs, outputs, and official cases to split the problem into smaller signal relationships."

msgid "hardware.hint.tutorial.1"
msgstr "Build one shortest signal chain: start at an output port and watch the signal follow the exact displayed wire to its target."

msgid "hardware.hint.tutorial.2"
msgstr "Try sending input A through NOT and then into the lamp; watch the port colors before and after inversion."

msgid "hardware.hint.tutorial.3"
msgstr "The complete example uses A → NOT → LAMP, enough to practice connecting, running, deleting, and reconnecting."

msgid "hardware.hint.half_adder.1"
msgstr "Draw separate four-row truth tables for SUM and CARRY. Look at one output at a time and find which input combinations make it 1."

msgid "hardware.hint.half_adder.2"
msgstr "SUM is 1 when the inputs differ. The hint board shows the (A OR B) AND NOT(A AND B) result path."

msgid "hardware.hint.half_adder.3"
msgstr "The complete answer adds A AND B as CARRY beside the SUM path; both outputs share A and B."

msgid "hardware.hint.full_adder.1"
msgstr "Add A and B first, then add the first SUM to CIN; finally decide how the two carry results combine."

msgid "hardware.hint.full_adder.2"
msgstr "The key path chains two HalfAdders, and the second HalfAdder's SUM becomes the final SUM."

msgid "hardware.hint.full_adder.3"
msgstr "The complete answer also ORs the two HalfAdder CARRY outputs to produce COUT."

msgid "hardware.hint.alu.1"
msgstr "Produce candidate operations in parallel, then select one with the opcode; do not make the opcode change the operators themselves."

msgid "hardware.hint.alu.2"
msgstr "The key subcircuit shows AND, OR, NOT, and addition results entering a mux selected by OP0/OP1."

msgid "hardware.hint.alu.3"
msgstr "The complete answer connects all four candidates, selectors, RESULT, and the adder's separate CARRY output."

msgid "hardware.hint.latch.1"
msgstr "Two NOR gates can read each other's output and retain state while S=R=0; avoid asserting S and R together."

msgid "hardware.hint.latch.2"
msgstr "The key subcircuit shows the two NOR cross-feedback wires and which side receives S and R."

msgid "hardware.hint.latch.3"
msgstr "The complete answer connects the cross-coupled NOR outputs to Q and NQ."

msgid "hardware.hint.register.1"
msgstr "LOAD=0 must preserve the latch; with LOAD=1, D and NOT D should form SET and RESET."

msgid "hardware.hint.register.2"
msgstr "The key subcircuit uses two AND gates to combine LOAD with D and NOT D before the SRLatch."

msgid "hardware.hint.register.3"
msgstr "The complete answer feeds both gated paths into the SRLatch and connects its Q to the level output."

msgid "hardware.hint.ram.1"
msgstr "Separate writing from reading: a decoder enables only the addressed register, while a mux reads the addressed row."

msgid "hardware.hint.ram.2"
msgstr "The key subcircuit sends ADDR/WRITE into the decoder and drives the two Register4 LOAD inputs separately."

msgid "hardware.hint.ram.3"
msgstr "The complete answer also fans DATA to both registers and uses ADDR to select the word mux output."

msgid "hardware.hint.cpu.1"
msgstr "Draw the data path first: where ACC, immediate values, and RAM data meet; then let CONTROL only select, load, and write."

msgid "hardware.hint.cpu.2"
msgstr "The key subcircuit shows the main CONTROL, SOURCE_MUX, ALU, RESULT_MUX, and ACC data loop."

msgid "hardware.hint.cpu.3"
msgstr "The complete answer adds RAM addressing/writes and both external probes to form the program-capable TinyComputer."

msgid "hardware.hint.load_store.1"
msgstr "Trace OP, ARG, and ADDR one instruction at a time, recording ACC and the addressed memory row before and after each step."

msgid "hardware.hint.load_store.2"
msgstr "The key connections feed all three Test Bench inputs into TinyComputer; first verify every width and port order."

msgid "hardware.hint.load_store.3"
msgstr "The complete reference also connects ACC and MEM outputs; this topology is fixed, so focus on reading state changes."

