msgid "system.level.assembly.title"
msgstr "CONNECT THE FIRST SYSTEM"

msgid "system.level.assembly.description"
msgstr "Join the player-provenance CPU8, 8-bit Bus, and RAM64x8 into one runnable computer."

msgid "system.level.assembly.objective"
msgstr "Connect all six request, write, and read routes, apply the program, and pass both official cases."

msgid "system.level.cpu_speed.title"
msgstr "AFTER THE CPU GETS FASTER"

msgid "system.level.cpu_speed.description"
msgstr "This memory-heavy sum mixes arithmetic with repeated data trips. Predict whether 4× faster arithmetic makes the whole run 4× faster, then test it."

msgid "system.level.cpu_speed.objective"
msgstr "Lock a prediction, run Eco as the baseline, then change only CPU to Fast and explain total-cycle change from compute versus WAIT."

msgid "system.level.ram_wait.title"
msgstr "WHO IS THE CPU WAITING FOR?"

msgid "system.level.ram_wait.description"
msgstr "Predict where CPU time goes, then follow repeated requests, RAM service, returned data, and the CPU's visible WAIT state."

msgid "system.level.ram_wait.objective"
msgstr "Lock a prediction, keep CPU, Bus, program, and tests fixed, then change only RAM and explain the CPU-wait delta."

msgid "system.level.bus_width.title"
msgstr "HOW MANY TRIPS FOR ONE BYTE?"

msgid "system.level.bus_width.description"
msgstr "The same byte crosses each Bus width; predict how serialization changes, then count the stages on the exact wire."

msgid "system.level.bus_width.objective"
msgstr "Lock a prediction, run Bus2 as the baseline, then change only Bus width and inspect segmented packets on the exact wires."

msgid "system.level.bottleneck.title"
msgstr "BOTTLENECK INVESTIGATION"

msgid "system.level.bottleneck.description"
msgstr "Investigate one exact system across 4, 16, and 64 items. Use raw totals, CPU WAIT, workload growth, and Trace flow before the full breakdown is revealed."

msgid "system.level.bottleneck.objective"
msgstr "Pass the 4/16/64 official cases, submit CPU, RAM, Bus, or mixed as your first diagnosis, then compare it with the revealed breakdown."

