msgid "hardware.completion.chapter"
msgstr "Hardware Foundations · Prologue"

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.tutorial"
msgstr "You learned ports, levels, wiring, removal, and reconnection. The visible wires on the workbench are the topology the circuit really executes."

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.half_adder"
msgstr "You separated two inputs into SUM and CARRY, then sealed the gate circuit you built as your reusable HalfAdder."

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.full_adder"
msgstr "You combined smaller adders to handle carry-in, using an owned abstraction to construct a higher-level component for the first time."

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.alu"
msgstr "You used control signals to select arithmetic results and saw how an ALU brings several operations into one data path."

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.latch"
msgstr "You stored state through feedback and discovered the boundary between combinational logic and a component with memory."

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.register"
msgstr "You used LOAD to control when new data is accepted and turned one-bit storage into a reusable register abstraction."

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.ram"
msgstr "You combined address, write control, and data ports into addressable memory, observing write, hold, and read state changes."

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.cpu"
msgstr "You joined an ALU, registers, control, and RAM into a small computer and took ownership of a complete data path."

msgid "hardware.completion.summary.load_store"
msgstr "You made the CPU reach external memory through LOAD and STORE, exposing the boundary where the processor must wait for data to return."

msgid "system.completion.chapter"
msgstr "Chapter 1 · Waiting for Data"

msgid "system.completion.summary.assembly"
msgstr "You connected the CPU, Bus, and RAM request, write, and read routes, proving that the displayed wires are the system topology."

msgid "system.completion.summary.cpu_speed"
msgstr "Your prediction met a controlled surprise: Eco → Fast made arithmetic 4× faster, but unchanged CPU WAIT limited total improvement to about 15%."

msgid "system.completion.summary.ram_wait"
msgstr "After predicting the balance, you changed only RAM and traced storage service directly into the CPU-wait delta."

msgid "system.completion.summary.bus_width"
msgstr "After predicting the packet change, you held every other condition fixed and watched one byte's four Bus2 data stages become one on Bus8."

msgid "system.completion.summary.bottleneck"
msgstr "You used raw Trace, CPU WAIT, and 4/16/64 growth evidence to commit a diagnosis before checking the revealed CPU/RAM/Bus breakdown."

